BlastmasterOS — Build and Installation Notes
=============================================

BlastmasterOS is an experimental operating system based on the ReactOS
codebase. The system is alpha quality. Features may be incomplete, and
installation or use may cause data loss.

IMPORTANT SAFETY NOTICE
-----------------------

Test in a virtual machine using a disposable virtual disk. Do not install
BlastmasterOS on a computer or disk containing important data. Verify the
target disk carefully before allowing setup to modify partitions.

1. Build environment
--------------------

The repository uses CMake, Ninja, and platform-specific toolchains. The root
CMakePresets.json lists the provided build presets. Required compilers and
additional tools depend on the chosen host platform and architecture.

Useful references:
  https://cmake.org/
  https://ninja-build.org/
  https://reactos.org/wiki/Building_ReactOS

2. Inspect available presets
----------------------------

From the repository root, run:

  cmake --list-presets

Choose a preset that matches your host toolchain and target architecture.
Preset names and output directories are defined in CMakePresets.json and may
change over time.

3. Configure and build
----------------------

For example, if the listed preset is mingw-i386-debug:

  cmake --preset mingw-i386-debug
  cmake --build output-MinGW-i386

Use the actual preset and binary directory listed in your checkout. A full
build may take considerable time and disk space.

4. Create a bootable ISO
------------------------

After configuration and a successful build, run the bootcd target against
the selected build directory. For the example above:

  cmake --build output-MinGW-i386 --target bootcd

Check the build output to determine the exact ISO filename and location.
Do not assume the ISO is bootable merely because the build command succeeds.

5. Test before installation
---------------------------

Boot the ISO in a virtual machine before attempting installation. Verify that
the boot process reaches setup, that setup behaves as expected, and that the
installed system can restart and boot from its virtual disk. Record failures
and relevant logs.

Use a disposable virtual disk. Do not use a disk containing important data.

6. Project and licensing information
------------------------------------

BlastmasterOS is an independent project based on the ReactOS codebase. It is
not an official ReactOS release. The underlying code and third-party
components remain subject to their respective licenses and notices.

Review COPYING, CREDITS, and component-level license files before
redistributing source or binaries. Keep applicable copyright notices and
attribution intact.

For upstream build-system background, consult:
  https://reactos.org/wiki/Building_ReactOS
